<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Q2 current account surplus 103 mln punts.</title>
<headline>Irish Q2 current account surplus 103 mln punts.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's current account surplus was a preliminary 103 million punts in the second quarter of 1996 versus a surplus of 314 million in the second quarter last year, Central Statistics Office figures showed on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				  1996 Q2    1995 Q2    1995 year</p>
<p> Current account	    103	  314	  981</p>
<p> Merchandise		  1978	 1910	 7340</p>
<p> Invisibles		  -1874	-1596	-6359</p>
<p> Cap and fin account	10	  -1221	-1329</p>
<p>(figures in millions of punts)</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
